5️⃣ Bill Pugh Singleton (Initialization-on-Demand Holder)

⭐ Most Recommended (Interview Favorite)

Concept

 Uses static inner class
 JVM loads inner class only when accessed

Code

java
public class BillPughSingleton {

    private BillPughSingleton() { }

    private static class SingletonHelper {
        private static final BillPughSingleton INSTANCE =
                new BillPughSingleton();
    }

    public static BillPughSingleton getInstance() {
        return SingletonHelper.INSTANCE;
    }
}

public class BillPughSingleton {
	private BillPughSingleton(){}
	
	private static class SingletonHelper {
		private static final BillPughSingleton INSTANCE = new BillPughSingleton();
	}
	
	public static BillPughSingleton getInstance() {
		return SingletonHelper.INSTANCE;
	}
}

✅ Pros

 Lazy initialization
 Thread-safe
 No synchronization overhead

📌 Use when

 You want clean, efficient, production-ready singleton

---

6️⃣ Enum Singleton (Best & Safest)

⭐⭐⭐ Best Solution (Joshua Bloch Recommended)

Concept

 Enum ensures:

   Single instance
   Serialization safety
   Reflection attack protection

Code

java
public enum EnumSingleton {
    INSTANCE;

    public void doSomething() {
        System.out.println("Singleton via Enum");
    }
}


✅ Pros

 Thread-safe
 Serialization safe
 Reflection safe
 Very simple

❌ Cons

 Cannot extend classes
 Less flexible (some frameworks dislike enums)

📌 Use when

 You want absolute safety
 Configuration managers, constants, utilities

---

7️⃣ Singleton with Serialization Protection

Problem

Serialization can break singleton:

java
ObjectInputStream -> creates NEW instance


Solution

Implement readResolve()

java
protected Object readResolve() {
    return getInstance();
}


---

8️⃣ Singleton with Reflection Protection

Problem

Reflection can access private constructor

Solution

java
private Singleton() {
    if (instance != null) {
        throw new RuntimeException("Use getInstance()");
    }
}


